WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.754
Most visual question answering models are black
boxes: they output an answer,

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:07.588
but not the reasoning that produced it.

00:00:07.668 --> 00:00:11.422
This paper,

00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:15.257
Towards Reasoning-Aware Explainable VQA from the
University of Illinois and Amazon Alexa AI,

00:00:15.337 --> 00:00:19.091
augments a state-of-the-art coarse-to-fine VQA
backbone with an end-to-end explanation generation module,

00:00:19.171 --> 00:00:22.925
so the model produces a human-readable textual
explanation alongside every answer while

00:00:23.005 --> 00:00:26.759
keeping accuracy essentially unchanged.

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:30.593
It compares LSTM and Transformer decoders as the
explanation generator, and,

00:00:30.673 --> 00:00:34.428
crucially,

00:00:34.508 --> 00:00:38.262
shows through a large human study that the standard
string-matching metrics like BLEU

00:00:38.342 --> 00:00:42.096
and ROUGE are unreliable for judging explanations,

00:00:42.176 --> 00:00:45.930
motivating better evaluation.
